IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore) -- section 7, interests in shares.
--
-- Section 7 is the Act's answer to "who counts as owning shares". It is cited by
-- Division 4 of Part 4 (directors' and substantial shareholders' disclosure), and
-- by ss 163 to 165 and 244.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- THE MODEL. A person's own interest in a given set of shares is decided from the
-- facts about that person (s 7(1A), (2), (3), (6), (6A), (9)). Section 7(4) and (4A)
-- then pass an interest upwards through bodies corporate, one tier at a time; the
-- chain of tiers is a list, and the interest reaches the top only if every tier
-- triggers.

§ `Companies Act 1967 -- section 7`

§§ `7(1) -- where section 7 has effect at all`

-- s 7(1): "The following subsections have effect for the purposes of Division 4 of
-- Part 4 and sections 163, 164 and 165 and SUBSECTION (6A), IN ADDITION, ALSO has
-- effect for the purposes of section 244."
--
-- So for section 244 only subsection (6A), the book-entry rule, applies. The other
-- subsections of section 7 have no effect there, and section 244 has to find its
-- notion of an interest in shares elsewhere.
DECLARE ProvisionUsingInterests IS ONE OF
    `Division 4 of Part 4`
    `section 163`
    `section 164`
    `section 165`
    `section 244`
    `some other provision`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A ProvisionUsingInterests
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 as a whole has effect for this provision` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `Division 4 of Part 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 163` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 164` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 165` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A ProvisionUsingInterests
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (6A) has effect for this provision` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `some other provision` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7(1A), (1B), (2), (3), (6), (6A), (7), (8), (9), (10) -- a person's own interest`

-- s 7(1A): "a person has an interest in shares if the person has AUTHORITY (whether
-- formal or informal, or express or implied) to DISPOSE OF, or to EXERCISE CONTROL OVER
-- THE DISPOSAL OF, those shares."
-- s 7(1B): "it is immaterial ... that the authority ... is, or is capable of being made,
-- SUBJECT TO RESTRAINT OR RESTRICTION."
-- s 7(2): "Where any property held in trust consists of or includes shares and a
-- person KNOWS, OR HAS REASONABLE GROUNDS FOR BELIEVING, that the person has an interest
-- under the trust, the person is deemed to have an interest in those shares."
-- s 7(3): a unit in a collective investment scheme that is the subject of an offer
-- and has been subscribed or purchased, or is issued for the purpose of an offer and
-- held by the manager, "does not constitute an interest in a share".
-- s 7(6): a person is deemed to have an interest in a share where the person --
--   (a) has entered into a CONTRACT TO PURCHASE a share;
--   (b) has a RIGHT, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to
--       have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order, whether
--       presently exercisable or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a
--       condition or not;
--   (c) has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an
--       OPTION, whether exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the
--       fulfilment of a condition or not; or
--   (d) is entitled (otherwise than by reason of having been appointed a PROXY or
--       representative to vote at a meeting) to exercise or control the exercise of a
--       right attached to a share, not being a share of which the person is the
--       registered holder.
-- s 7(6A): a book-entry security is treated as if it were an interest in a share.
-- s 7(7): joint holding with another does not negate the interest.
-- s 7(8): it is immaterial that the interest cannot be related to a particular share.
-- s 7(9): "There is to be DISREGARDED --
--   (a) an interest in a share if the interest is that of a person who holds the share
--       as BARE TRUSTEE;
--   (b) an interest in a share if the interest is that of a person whose ordinary
--       business includes the LENDING OF MONEY if the person holds the interest only
--       by way of SECURITY for the purposes of a transaction entered into in the
--       ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money;
--   (c) an interest of a person in a share, if that interest is an interest held by
--       the person by reason of the person holding a PRESCRIBED OFFICE;
--   (ca) an interest of a company in its OWN SHARES if that interest is purchased or
--        otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including
--        TREASURY SHARES); and
--   (d) a PRESCRIBED interest."
-- s 7(10): an interest "is not to be disregarded by reason only of -- (a) its
-- remoteness; (b) the manner in which it arose; or (c) the fact that the exercise of a
-- right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint
-- or restriction."
DECLARE PersonsInterest HAS
    `has authority, formal or informal, express or implied, to dispose of the shares or to control their disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or has reasonable grounds for believing it has an interest under a trust whose property includes the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has contracted to purchase a share` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a right, other than as a trust beneficiary, to have a share transferred to it or its order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a right to acquire a share or an interest in a share under an option` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share it is not the registered holder of, other than as proxy or representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a book-entry security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interest is a unit in a collective investment scheme within section 7(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds the share as bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lends money in the ordinary course of business and holds the interest only as security for such a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a company's interest in its own shares bought or acquired under sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a prescribed interest to be disregarded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds jointly with another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interest cannot be related to any particular share` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interest is remote, or arose in an unusual way, or is subject to restraint` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the interest` IS A PersonsInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is within a limb of section 7 that gives an interest` IF
        `the interest`'s `has authority, formal or informal, express or implied, to dispose of the shares or to control their disposal`
    OR  `the interest`'s `knows or has reasonable grounds for believing it has an interest under a trust whose property includes the shares`
    OR  `the interest`'s `has contracted to purchase a share`
    OR  `the interest`'s `has a right, other than as a trust beneficiary, to have a share transferred to it or its order`
    OR  `the interest`'s `has a right to acquire a share or an interest in a share under an option`
    OR  `the interest`'s `is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share it is not the registered holder of, other than as proxy or representative`
    OR  `the interest`'s `holds a book-entry security`

GIVEN `the interest` IS A PersonsInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is disregarded under section 7(9)` IF
        `the interest`'s `holds the share as bare trustee`
    OR  `the interest`'s `lends money in the ordinary course of business and holds the interest only as security for such a transaction`
    OR  `the interest`'s `holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office`
    OR  `the interest`'s `is a company's interest in its own shares bought or acquired under sections 76B to 76G`
    OR  `the interest`'s `is a prescribed interest to be disregarded`

-- s 7(3) is expressed as a thing that "does not constitute an interest in a share",
-- so it removes the interest before section 7(9) is reached. The three things s 7(7),
-- (8) and (10) say are immaterial are fields that no rule reads, and the cases
-- assert that varying them changes nothing.
GIVEN `the interest` IS A PersonsInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has an interest in the shares on its own account` IF
        NOT `the interest`'s `the interest is a unit in a collective investment scheme within section 7(3)`
    AND `the interest is within a limb of section 7 that gives an interest` `the interest`
    AND NOT `the interest is disregarded under section 7(9)` `the interest`

-- s 7(6A) says a book-entry security is treated as if it were an interest in a share.
-- The disregard in s 7(9)(a) therefore reaches a person who holds a book-entry
-- security as bare trustee. Whether the Depository's holding of book-entry securities
-- as bare trustee is disregarded for section 244 under (9)(a) is the question the
-- cases ask of it; the Act does not say, because section 7 as a whole does not apply
-- for section 244.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holding jointly with another person prevents an interest` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `being unable to relate the interest to a particular share prevents an interest` IF
    FALSE

§§ `7(4), 7(4A), 7(5) -- an interest passes upwards through bodies corporate`

-- s 7(4): "Where a body corporate has, or is by the provisions of this section deemed
-- to have, an interest in a share and --
--   (a) the body corporate is, or its directors are, ACCUSTOMED OR UNDER AN
--       OBLIGATION whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the
--       directions, instructions or wishes of a person; or
--   (b) a person has a CONTROLLING INTEREST in the body corporate,
-- that person is deemed to have an interest in that share."
-- s 7(4A): "Where a body corporate has, or is by the provisions of this section (apart
-- from this subsection) deemed to have, an interest in a share and --
--   (a) a person is; (b) the associates of a person are; or (c) a person and the
--   person's associates are,
-- entitled to exercise or control the exercise of NOT LESS THAN 20% of the VOTING POWER
-- in the body corporate, that person is deemed to have an interest in that share."
-- s 7(5): "a person is an associate of another person if the firstmentioned person is --
--   (a) a SUBSIDIARY of that other person;
--   (b) a person who is accustomed or is under an obligation whether formal or informal
--       to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of that other
--       person IN RELATION TO THE SHARE mentioned in subsection (4A); or
--   (c) a BODY CORPORATE that is, or a majority of the directors of which are, accustomed
--       or under an obligation ... to act in accordance with the directions, instructions
--       or wishes of that other person in relation to the share".
--
-- THE LOOK-THROUGH THIS PRODUCES. Each upward step is tested against the voting power in
-- the IMMEDIATE body corporate only, and a deemed interest is itself an interest that
-- the next step can start from. So a person holding 20% of A, which holds 20% of B,
-- which holds 20% of C, which holds the shares, is deemed to have an interest in the
-- shares, although their economic stake is 0.8%. The threshold is not compounded along
-- the chain. The cases assert exactly that.
--
-- "Controlling interest" in s 7(4)(b) is not defined in section 7. The encoding takes
-- it as a supplied fact.
DECLARE HowAssociated IS ONE OF
    `a subsidiary of the person`
    `a person accustomed or obliged to act on the person's wishes in relation to the share`
    `a body corporate, or one whose majority of directors are, so accustomed or obliged`
    `not an associate within section 7(5)`

DECLARE Associate HAS
    `how associated` IS A HowAssociated
    `voting power in the body corporate, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the associates` IS A LIST OF Associate
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the voting power the associates control` IS
    CONSIDER `the associates`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `a` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN (CONSIDER `a`'s `how associated`
              WHEN `not an associate within section 7(5)` THEN 0
              OTHERWISE `a`'s `voting power in the body corporate, as a percentage`)
             PLUS `the voting power the associates control` `rest`

DECLARE Tier HAS
    `the body corporate or its directors are accustomed or obliged to act on this person's directions, instructions or wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person has a controlling interest in the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the voting power this person is entitled to exercise or control, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `the associates of this person` IS A LIST OF Associate

GIVEN `the tier` IS A Tier
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the voting power the person and the person's associates control together` IS
    `the tier`'s `the voting power this person is entitled to exercise or control, as a percentage`
        PLUS `the voting power the associates control` (`the tier`'s `the associates of this person`)

GIVEN `the tier` IS A Tier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this tier passes the interest upwards` IF
        `the tier`'s `the body corporate or its directors are accustomed or obliged to act on this person's directions, instructions or wishes`
    OR  `the tier`'s `this person has a controlling interest in the body corporate`
    OR  `the voting power the person and the person's associates control together` `the tier` AT LEAST 20

GIVEN `the tiers` IS A LIST OF Tier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every tier passes the interest upwards` IS
    CONSIDER `the tiers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `t` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     `this tier passes the interest upwards` `t`
             AND `every tier passes the interest upwards` `rest`

-- The person at the top has an interest if the body corporate at the bottom has one
-- that is not disregarded, and every step between them passes it up. If the
-- bottom-tier interest is one that s 7(9) disregards, it is not an interest for the
-- purposes of s 7(4) and (4A) either; that is the natural reading of "to be
-- disregarded", and the Act does not address the point.
GIVEN `the bottom interest` IS A PersonsInterest, `the chain above it` IS A LIST OF Tier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person at the top of the chain has an interest in the shares` IF
        `the person has an interest in the shares on its own account` `the bottom interest`
    AND `every tier passes the interest upwards` `the chain above it`
